  "evidence_boundary": "Read-only bridge diagnostic for ship post-capture continuations whose factual next opponent is absent from the ordinary per-ship position adapter solely because its T-1 mission is Tow or Intercept. It builds owner-current T-1 GameState and runs the existing production movement phases in Host order Tow -> Move Most -> Intercept. A target-side outbound transfer is applied only as a bounded hypothesis when it is a fully observable co-located same-owner ship transfer with sufficient sender cargo and receiver capacity. For a co-located foreign ship transfer, legality/receiver semantics remain unresolved; instead the diagnostic runs both the no-transfer and sender-reduced movement bounds and accepts geometry only when target and interceptor endpoints are identical and both interceptor endpoints equal the held-out factual combat site. Other ambiguous transfers, MKT mass changes, mine-risk routes, unresolved warp-well context and HYP intercept targets fail closed. Factual combat-site coordinates are used only as the held-out comparator. This diagnostic does not alter combat selection and does not yet claim full movement-pipeline closure for ion-storm/chunnel/special-movement combinations.",
